{
  "_readme": [
    "Screenshot caption copy per locale, used to stamp out marketing/aso/<locale>/<platform>/params.yaml.",
    "",
    "These are MARKETING lines, not translations. Each is rewritten to be short and idiomatic in its",
    "own language, because the title renders as large display text: a literal German rendering of",
    "'Twenty-six audio tools, one app' runs off the canvas, so the German line counts differently.",
    "Meaning is preserved; wording is not.",
    "",
    "NEVER translated, in any locale: Overtone Lab, and the tool surnames and standards that are the",
    "product's credibility — Sabine, Partch, Thiele, Thiele-Small, Butterworth, Fletcher, Blumlein,",
    "ORTF, NOS, RT60, LUFS, ITU-R BS.1770, Schroeder, Tenney. Units stay symbols: Hz, dB, m³.",
    "",
    "Media locales are the 5 the store gets images for. Every other shipped language inherits the",
    "primary language's screenshots by Apple's own default, so shooting all 17 would only buy a",
    "maintenance tax on every future UI change.",
    "",
    "ios has 6 captions, ipad and mac have 4 — matching the raw capture sets.",
    "",
    "Japanese titles must be SHORT: with no spaces, wrap_text cannot break them, so a long line renders as one line and runs off the canvas instead of wrapping. Measure the rendered PNG (bright-pixel column span vs canvas width), do not trust the caption's character count."
  ],
